/-- **Cassels, Chapter 9, Example 21** (0-based indices): with $N_j(a)$ the number of integer representations of $a$
by $f_j$ ($f_1, f_2$ as printed; $f_3$ with the corrected sign `ex21f3`, see the module docstring),
